%I A399931 #9 Sep 22 2026 08:42:00
%S A399931 1,1,1,1,1,2,2,6,6,14,14,37,37
%N A399931 Maximum number of Hamiltonian cycles in a polyomino with 2*n cells.
%C A399931 The cycles pass from a cell to a neighboring cell, visiting each cell exactly once.
%C A399931 We follow the convention that K_2 has 1 Hamiltonian cycle, so a(1) = 1.
%C A399931 It is not always the case that either a(n) = a(k)*a(n-k) for some 1 <= k <= n-1 or a(n) = A321172(d,2*n/d) for d = A033676(2*n) (cf. formulas below). If that were the case, we would have a(14) = max(a(1)*a(13),A321172(4,7)) = max(37,92) = 92, a(15) = max(92,154) = 154, a(16) = max(154,236) = 236, and a(17) = max(236,1) = 236. But the 34-celled polyomino obtained from a 6 X 6 rectangle by removing a corner cell and one of its neighbors has 348 Hamiltonian cycles, so a(17) >= 348.
%H A399931 <a href="/index/Pol#polyominoes">Index entries for sequences related to polyominoes</a>.
%F A399931 a(n) >= a(k)*a(n-k) for 1 <= k <= n-1. Proof: Let P and Q be polyominoes with 2*k and 2*(n-k) cells, respectively, both with the maximum number of Hamiltonian cycles for their respective sizes. If P or Q has only 2 cells we assume that the cells are on top of each other in the vertical direction. Let (x,y) be the top cell in the rightmost column of P. Then (x,y-1) must also be a cell and (x,y-1) - (x,y) must be part of any Hamiltonian cycle in P. By translating Q, we can assume that the top cell in the leftmost column of Q is (x+1,y) and, by construction, P and Q do not overlap so the union R of P and Q is a polyomino with 2*n cells. Any Hamiltonian cycle in Q must contain (x+1,y-1) - (x+1,y). From any pair of Hamiltonian cycles in P and Q we can construct a unique Hamiltonian cycle in R by replacing (x,y-1) - (x,y) and (x+1,y-1) - (x+1,y) with (x,y) - (x+1,y) and (x,y-1) - (x+1,y-1), which proves that R has at least a(k)*a(n-k) Hamiltonian cycles.
%F A399931 a(n) >= A321172(d,2*n/d) for any proper divisor d of 2*n. (Presumably, the right hand side is largest when d = A033676(2*n).)
%Y A399931 Cf. A000105, A002931, A033676, A321172, A361288, A399932, A399933.
%K A399931 nonn,more,new
%O A399931 1,6
